{"event_type":"review","id":"b61e3d4de0575b18834c42d28177bcb869cb758c616cf95f7ea0ba7eade61726","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T17:05:33Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/29e6343e825c9028bf5aaf2f94334345660c2aa63b814c7702e3da1225e8e770","sha256":"29e6343e825c9028bf5aaf2f94334345660c2aa63b814c7702e3da1225e8e770"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0d09661432c0442ab2387acf4dc5c755136912c1fe5a45898101c7c79def36d8","sha256":"0d09661432c0442ab2387acf4dc5c755136912c1fe5a45898101c7c79def36d8"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c0f6348e156d6905fe830e7fce1576bf83d1e93405d36393b24f0a32682bfdd8","sha256":"c0f6348e156d6905fe830e7fce1576bf83d1e93405d36393b24f0a32682bfdd8"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ed41373041ce86c8bfe5e666684a3e605d0b11ad50a4c40de75a09cc4b3ef664","sha256":"ed41373041ce86c8bfe5e666684a3e605d0b11ad50a4c40de75a09cc4b3ef664"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/273a1d96859031f64d82a50a55c18404f548115d46b30cab961ad4dc030d8fa1","sha256":"273a1d96859031f64d82a50a55c18404f548115d46b30cab961ad4dc030d8fa1"}],"attempt_id":"1e5df40a6179b7e7f2b6b7a407d820925f3ce07e32a25e85898cd846b7dd59e8:0:1","base":"e6ca37eba48f9216486cc714e33d0c798dd30081","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"0e0dcd740d731899ab6874759f9466b85c9ea592","body":"**Correct the endpoint description.**\n\n`docs/dd-1-abort-spike.md:34` says both lanes use the anthropic-compatible endpoint. Lines 40 and 54–56 identify a different OpenAI-compatible endpoint for `ai-sdk`. This can misdirect endpoint configuration and outage diagnosis. Describe each lane’s endpoint separately.","id":"0b68e21fb65339b97d77ac58a7c9b6a6d1e0f4fb6798f5c611a2eeef32ddbfab","intervals":[],"path":"docs/dd-1-abort-spike.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Correct the endpoint description."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"678fed3c8451129665e22b58ddd7f5de22410caa","body":"**Do not treat the tool-call stream as a complete security backstop.**\n\nACP recommends reporting tool calls but does not require it. An agent can execute a tool without sending either a permission request or a `tool_call`, leaving this tripwire with no evidence. Restrict this guarantee to endpoints whose enforcement is independently established, or provide an independent containment boundary. ([agentclientprotocol.com](https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/v1/tool-calls))","id":"5c21ab1104e4dddf1085a88536ccb0447058de9c49b7694441e7a938143059e9","intervals":[],"path":"docs/acp-driver.md","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not treat the tool-call stream as a complete security backstop."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"9f57bf1cab2a56c472d5814b46a4784643ccb077","body":"**Do not assume `allow_always` is confined to one run.**\n\nThe agent controls the scope and lifetime of a remembered decision. It can apply a project-wide approval to later calls without asking again, including calls outside the allowlist. A later tripwire cannot undo an executed tool. Reject `allow_always` unless its scope is known to preserve the policy. ([agentclientprotocol.com](https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/v1/tool-calls))","id":"3d38e4625251773ff66560f8862911066fa1ac6fcbee42dcbda15f236ae27305","intervals":[],"path":"docs/acp-driver-strategy.md","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not assume `allowalways` is confined to one run."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"678fed3c8451129665e22b58ddd7f5de22410caa","body":"**Accept the config-option response as pin evidence.**\n\nACP returns current values in `configOptions`. A compliant agent can return `mode: build` there without sending a `current_mode_update`. This rule would reject that successful pin before every prompt. Include the returned config option in the verification rule. ([agentclientprotocol.com](https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/v1/schema))","id":"ceeb01e3efa224e5ff2a1a6c7b896b02ad681a072ccacd3b8a3b0b03168531c5","intervals":[],"path":"docs/acp-driver.md","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Accept the config-option response as pin evidence."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"9f57bf1cab2a56c472d5814b46a4784643ccb077","body":"**Do not classify a pending tool call as executed.**\n\nACP permits a `tool_call` in `pending` state while input is streaming or approval is pending. An agent can report that call before sending its permission request, so this rule would mark a governed call as ungated and fail the run. Track the call through its permission and execution states instead. ([agentclientprotocol.com](https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/v1/tool-calls))","id":"ead122eefa3b0d41679e03fc304cfb4cda257d888dfe1341be0e01b501fb50f8","intervals":[],"path":"docs/acp-driver-strategy.md","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Do not classify a pending tool call as executed."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"678fed3c8451129665e22b58ddd7f5de22410caa","body":"**Clarify the cancellation exception in the permission rules.**\n\n`docs/acp-driver.md:121` and `docs/acp-driver-strategy.md:264` say the driver never answers `cancelled`, but the strategy later describes that outcome on cancellation. Clarify that policy denials do not use `cancelled` and document ACP’s requirement for pending requests when the turn is cancelled.","id":"ca4778d24f486599f9c771cdd0296e7388a9272af23aa834456d284d15cd4b3c","intervals":[],"path":"docs/acp-driver.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Clarify the cancellation exception in the permission rules."}],"head":"5508faf6036ca0c87688a4f09cc50115941238ac","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"9dd38cfa05b84191e6dddf293a8b826e957050e9","intervals":[[1,4]],"path":"CLAUDE.md"},{"blob":"9f57bf1cab2a56c472d5814b46a4784643ccb077","intervals":[[1,812]],"path":"docs/acp-driver-strategy.md"},{"blob":"678fed3c8451129665e22b58ddd7f5de22410caa","intervals":[[1,190]],"path":"docs/acp-driver.md"},{"blob":"0e0dcd740d731899ab6874759f9466b85c9ea592","intervals":[[1,120]],"path":"docs/dd-1-abort-spike.md"},{"blob":"39903696fb1c04a940393baa227d9e14892b9444","intervals":[[1,176]],"path":"src/plans/registry.ts"},{"blob":"6ffcb0c56a0cff49d17267454b8b1155ffa1020e","intervals":[[1,401]],"path":"src/registry/index.ts"}],"job_id":"1e5df40a6179b7e7f2b6b7a407d820925f3ce07e32a25e85898cd846b7dd59e8:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"39903696fb1c04a940393baa227d9e14892b9444","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/plans/registry.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"6ffcb0c56a0cff49d17267454b8b1155ffa1020e","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/registry/index.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"9dd38cfa05b84191e6dddf293a8b826e957050e9","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"CLAUDE.md","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"9f57bf1cab2a56c472d5814b46a4784643ccb077","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"docs/acp-driver-strategy.md","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"678fed3c8451129665e22b58ddd7f5de22410caa","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"docs/acp-driver.md","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"residual uncovered lines"},"blob":"0e0dcd740d731899ab6874759f9466b85c